<fieldset><legend>Performance Dashboard</legend>
  <p><label for="settings_performance_delivery_target">Delivery Target (%)</label><%= number_field_tag 'settings[performance_delivery_target]', TicketJourney::PerformanceSettings.delivery_target(settings), id: 'settings_performance_delivery_target', min: 0, max: 100, step: 'any', required: true %> Default: 90%. Shared by Done Tickets / Due Tickets and Done Weight / Due Weight for all employees and projects. Changes also apply to past report dates; actual delivery percentages are unchanged.</p>
  <p>Configure existing numeric User custom fields. Create each field only if it does not already exist. No fields are created automatically.</p>
  <p>Day 0 is automatic: the owner's Redmine account creation date for monthly ticket count; the earliest eligible positive-weight ticket's Redmine Start date for monthly complexity weight. The former manual Day 0 setting is no longer used.</p>
  <% [['count', 'Expected Monthly Ticket Count'], ['weight', 'Expected Monthly Complexity Weight']].each do |key, label| %>
    <p><label for="settings_performance_<%= key %>_field_id"><%= label %></label><%= select_tag "settings[performance_#{key}_field_id]", options_for_select(UserCustomField.where(field_format: %w[int float]).order(:name).map { |f| ["#{f.name} (##{f.id})", f.id] }, settings["performance_#{key}_field_id"]), include_blank: 'Not configured', id: "settings_performance_#{key}_field_id" %></p>
  <% end %>
  <p>Only public monthly target fields are shown to non-administrators. Monthly employee targets are separate from the shared delivery percentage. No Extra Tasks adjustment applies.</p>
</fieldset>
